  /// Zone. SINGLE_AZ_HA_1 - Creates file systems with high availability and
  /// throughput capacities of 64 - 4,096 MB/s by deploying a primary and
  /// standby file system within the same Availability Zone. SINGLE_AZ_2 -
  /// Creates file systems with throughput capacities of 160 - 10,240 MB/s
  /// using an NVMe L2ARC cache that automatically recover within a single
  /// Availability Zone. SINGLE_AZ_1 - Creates file systems with throughput
  /// capacities of 64 - 4,096 MBs that automatically recover within a single
  /// Availability Zone. For a list of which Amazon Web Services Regions each
  /// deployment type is available in, see Deployment type availability . For
  /// more information on the differences in performance between deployment
  /// types, see File system performance in the Amazon FSx for OpenZFS User
  /// Guide .
  pub deployment_type: OpenZFSDeploymentType? = None
  /// Specifies the throughput of an Amazon FSx for OpenZFS file system,
  /// measured in megabytes per second (MBps). Valid values depend on the
  /// DeploymentType that you choose, as follows: For MULTI_AZ_1 and
  /// SINGLE_AZ_2 , valid values are 160, 320, 640, 1280, 2560, 3840, 5120,
  /// 7680, or 10240 MBps. For SINGLE_AZ_1 , valid values are 64, 128, 256,
  /// 512, 1024, 2048, 3072, or 4096 MBps. You pay for additional throughput
  /// capacity that you provision.
  pub throughput_capacity: Int? = None
  pub weekly_maintenance_start_time: Str? = None
  pub disk_iops_configuration: DiskIopsConfiguration? = None
  /// The configuration Amazon FSx uses when creating the root value of the
